 ### 3D Prior (Zero-1-to-3)
-3D Prior (Zero-1-to-3) uses Zero-1-to-3, a view-dependent diffusion model finetuned on Objaverse, as the 3D prior [S3, unofficial]. It takes a reference image $I_r$ and novel view camera poses $(R, T)$ as input to generate a novel view, thereby encouraging 3D consistency [S3, unofficial]. The 3D SDS loss is formulated as $\mathcal{L}_{3D} = \mathbb{E}_{t,\epsilon} w(t) \left( \frac{\partial I}{\partial \theta} \right) (\epsilon_\phi(z_t; I_r, t, R, T) - \epsilon)$ [S3, unofficial]. Unlike the 2D prior which uses text embedding, the 3D prior uses the reference view and camera poses as guidance to enable the usage of more 3D information [S3, unofficial].
