 ## Background
-Focaldreamer, also known as GSEditor-DDS and GSEditor-iN2N, is part of the latest series of methods that employ SDS loss within 3DGS to facilitate creative editing [S1]. It builds on the idea of using 3DGS for precise and flexible modifications. The method was introduced in the context of 3D editing surveys, highlighting the use of text prompts and discriminative masks for localized changes [S1]. It is related to other editing methods like TIP-Editor and CustomNeRF, but distinguishes itself by its specific use of normal maps and ellipsoids [S1].
